# How to add a custom lint rule to our ESLint plugin

This note walks through adding a rule called `no-bare-timeout` to the in-repo plugin under `tools/eslint-plugin-local/`. The rule flags calls to `setTimeout` whose delay argument is a numeric literal larger than 1000, so that long delays go through the shared `Delays` constants instead.

## 1. Create the rule file

Create `tools/eslint-plugin-local/rules/no-bare-timeout.js`:

```js
'use strict';

module.exports = {
  meta: {
    type: 'suggestion',
    docs: {
      description: 'disallow long literal delays passed to setTimeout',
    },
    schema: [
      {
        type: 'object',
        properties: { maxMs: { type: 'integer', minimum: 0 } },
        additionalProperties: false,
      },
    ],
    messages: {
      bare: 'Use a named constant from Delays instead of the literal {{value}}.',
    },
  },

  create(context) {
    const options = context.options[0] || {};
    const maxMs = options.maxMs === undefined ? 1000 : options.maxMs;

    return {
      CallExpression(node) {
        const callee = node.callee;
        const isSetTimeout =
          callee.type === 'Identifier' && callee.name === 'setTimeout';
        if (!isSetTimeout || node.arguments.length < 2) return;

        const delay = node.arguments[1];
        if (delay.type !== 'Literal' || typeof delay.value !== 'number') return;
        if (delay.value <= maxMs) return;

        context.report({
          node: delay,
          messageId: 'bare',
          data: { value: String(delay.value) },
        });
      },
    };
  },
};
```

## 2. Register it

Add the rule to the plugin index:

```js
module.exports = {
  rules: {
    'no-bare-timeout': require('./rules/no-bare-timeout'),
  },
};
```

Then turn it on in the root `.eslintrc.cjs`:

```js
rules: {
  'local/no-bare-timeout': ['warn', { maxMs: 1000 }],
},
```

## 3. Write tests

We use `RuleTester`. Put the file next to the rule as `no-bare-timeout.test.js`:

```js
const { RuleTester } = require('eslint');
const rule = require('./no-bare-timeout');

new RuleTester({ parserOptions: { ecmaVersion: 2022 } }).run('no-bare-timeout', rule, {
  valid: [
    'setTimeout(fn, 500)',
    'setTimeout(fn, Delays.RETRY)',
    { code: 'setTimeout(fn, 2500)', options: [{ maxMs: 5000 }] },
  ],
  invalid: [
    {
      code: 'setTimeout(fn, 3000)',
      errors: [{ messageId: 'bare', data: { value: '3000' } }],
    },
  ],
});
```

Run just this file with `npx jest tools/eslint-plugin-local/rules/no-bare-timeout.test.js`.

## 4. Things that tripped people up before

- `node.arguments[1]` can be a `TemplateLiteral` or a `BinaryExpression` such as `60 * 1000`. The rule above ignores those on purpose. If you want to catch constant folding, evaluate with `context.getScope()` helpers, but be aware that gets slow on large files.
- `window.setTimeout` and `globalThis.setTimeout` are `MemberExpression` callees and are not matched yet. Extend the check if your code base uses them.
- Autofix is intentionally absent. We cannot know which constant a delay should map to.
- When you change the message text, update the test data too, since `messageId` plus `data` is compared after interpolation.

## 5. Rolling out

Start as `warn`, wait one release, then promote to `error` once the warnings are cleaned up. Use `npx eslint . --rule 'local/no-bare-timeout: warn' -f json | jq '.[].messages | length'` to count the hits per file while you migrate.

